[Music]  starwars the last Jedi delivers a  soaring blend of drama action and comedy  while also tying up a few loose ends  left in the wake of the force awakens  writer director Rian Johnson chapter  successfully and perhaps controversial  thrusts the franchise forward in the  number of meaningful ways and it does so  largely by answering a few lingering  questions along the way  warning major spoilers ahead who are  Ray's parents it seems that in the Star  Wars universe all our favorite  characters are related in some way Darth  Vader was Luke's father Leia is Luke's  sister han Solo and Leia were married  for a time and kylo Ren also known as  Ben solo is there angsty villainous son  so when Rey was introduced in the force  awakens questions regarding her true  lineage ran rampant after years of  speculating that Rey was somehow related  to Luke Skywalker or obi-wan Kenobi the  last Jedi put all the rumors to bed in  one of the film's most subversive plot  twists Rey faces a deep truth about her  parents identities her parents were just  a couple of heartless and nobodies who  sold her off as a child of course this  bombshell could just be a red herring  but in a series that has become notable  for secret familial ties the notion that  Ray could be special just because she is  makes for a delightful change of pace  can Leia use force powers during the  credits of the last Jedi in loving  memory of our princess Carrie Fisher  appears on the screen while that  heartfelt goodbye acknowledges fishers  untimely passing the last Jedi story  does not but it does give her some  awesome powers early on kylo Ren leads  an attack on Leia ship there's a moment  when Leia senses her son's presence but  while he's successfully disposed of his  father in the force awakens kylo finds  himself unable to fire on his mother  instead his minions do the dirty work  and Leia's body is thrown into space but  it turns out that Leia is as tapped into  the forest as a brother and unbelievable  as it seems she uses the force to  navigate through the crushing vacuum of  space and back to safety back on her  ship Leia falls into a deep coma which  he remains in for the majority of the  film why does Luke want the Jedi to end  the ending of the force awakens found  Rey finally facing Luke Skywalker the  legendary Jedi who've gone and  hiding while fans were expecting an  emotional meeting between the two things  don't go down as planned when Ray finds  him on the planet where the first Jedi  Temple was built Skywalker takes his old  lightsaber and tosses it off a cliff why  is he so disdainful of the Jedi  it seems that Skywalker took the blame  for kylo ren's turned to the dark side  this all stems from Luke's failure to  train Ben solo in the ways of the force  when solo was a student Luke came close  to murdering him in his sleep because he  was frightened by the deep well of  darkness he sensed in the boy Ben woke  up to find Luke staring down at him with  lightsaber in hand and responded with a  fiery rage Ben destroyed the Jedi School  many of its students and assumed he'd  ended Skywalker in the process following  these events Luke decides he wants the  Jedi to end because theirs was a legacy  of hubris and failure capped by Luke's  own epic film which turned Ben solo into  kylo Ren and helped fuel the rise of the  first order  the snoke's identity even matter when  the force awakens hit theaters  speculation ran rampant regarding  supreme leader snoke s-- real identity  appearing only as a giant ominous  hologram Snoke was presented as  essentially the trilogy's new emperor  his motivations for turning kylo Ren  into the next Darth Vader helped fuel  the burning question who is this guy as  frustrating as it may be the last Jedi  doesn't deliver any new revelations on  that front what the movie does do is  finally give us smoke in the flesh as he  dishes out pain to kylo Hux and even Rey  before a surprise twist puts kylo and  Rey on the same team destroying Snoke  and splashy guards when all said and  done  it seems smokes true identity is well  just Snoke while it's likely his  backstory will be explored elsewhere as  far as the sequel trilogy is concerned  it seems we've learned all we need to  know about kylo ren's former master  thanks for watching click the looper  icon to subscribe to our YouTube channel  plus check out all this cool stuff we  know you love to  [Applause]  [Music]

